    "id": "episode-05-necessary-solutions",
    "title": "Episode 05: Necessary Solutions",
    "type": "Main story",
    "when": "Chapter 5",
    "summary": "Reunion takes Lungmen's headquarters. Ch'en retakes it after leaving Amiya's squad behind, and Hoshiguma is badly hurt holding back debris for her. Some supporting details are speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Aboard the Rhodes Island landship, Swire wakes Ch'en from a nightmare. Reunion has taken the Lungmen Guard Department headquarters, and Swire and Ch'en argue over who is to blame. Speculation: Swire blames Ch'en because she was knocked out in an ambush on the way back to Lungmen, and tells her she should resign as head of the Special Ops division. Then XR-02, Ch'en's informant, calls. Reunion has trapped him at the Muk Wo Warehouse, and he is holding time-sensitive intelligence.",
      "Ch'en speaks with a Rhodes Island officer about a joint attack, and reveals that she chose to protect Lungmen first. As a result, she left Amiya's squad behind in the abandoned Chernobog plate, and they are now listed as missing in action. Speculation (no source found yet): The officer leaves in disgust. Disputed: the draft said Ch'en decided not to ask Rhodes Island for help. Sources say she decided to ask Rhodes Island for help with the joint attack. Hoshiguma suspects that Wei Yenwu ordered the abandonment. Ch'en says that while she appreciates all he has done, she will never respect him.",
      "Ch'en and Hoshiguma raid the Muk Wo Warehouse. The informant is Phal, a man Hoshiguma has known for ten years, who infiltrated Reunion after becoming Infected. They break through and find him mortally wounded. The L.G.D. recovers the intelligence on his body anyway, and it indicates that Reunion's objective is not only a forward base in Lungmen but also a search for an extremely high-value individual.",
      "Ch'en's search leads her to the Ch'en Estate, the mansion of her biological father's clan. Reunion had broken into it before. She tells Hoshiguma she has no particular attachment to the place, but being inside its walls brings back memories. Inside, Ch'en finds a cracked photograph of herself and Talulah as children, hugging. Since Reunion had broken in before, she briefly wonders whether the photograph was what they were looking for.",
      "Next the L.G.D. captures Paci Plaza, a shopping mall owned by Swire's family and occupied by Reunion. During the fighting, an explosion collapses the floor beneath Ch'en. Hoshiguma holds the debris back with her shield so it doesn't crush them, and she is badly injured. She urges Ch'en to leave her behind, but Ch'en refuses. Ch'en admits she has changed since abandoning Amiya's squad, calls Hoshiguma her friend, and vows to be her shield. Later, Swire calls, angry about the damage to the mall, and Ch'en promises to buy her a meal.",
      "The L.G.D. enters the headquarters. Speculation (no source found yet): The building feels wrong, with many floors empty and Reunion forces barely prepared. Intelligence says Reunion's command center is on the roof, and Ch'en takes the bait. The roof is a trap set by Mephisto. Faust and his crossbowmen fire from range, and Mephisto uses his Arts to raise the dead Reunion soldiers as hulking monsters that resist physical damage. The Arts respond to Ch'en, which confuses him.",
      "Ch'en tries to draw Chi Xiao, the dragon-slaying sword. Speculation (no source found yet): Wei Yenwu once gave her the sword. Sources say that forcefully activating the Originium Arts inside the blade injures her. Speculation: The blast destroys several of Mephisto's puppets. Mephisto tries to recruit her to Reunion, and she refuses. Then reinforcements from Rhodes Island arrive on the Bad Guy with Amiya, the Doctor, and Blaze. Swire had secretly coordinated with Rhodes Island and rescued Amiya's squad from Chernobog. Speculation (no source found yet): Ch'en apologizes to Amiya for abandoning her.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Faust convinces Mephisto that the trap has failed, and they retreat. They destroy the rooftop behind them under cover of planted explosives. The L.G.D. recaptures its headquarters. Blaze confronts Wei Yenwu about using Rhodes Island and the L.G.D. as bait in Chernobog, and about ordering the abandonment of Amiya's team. Amiya talks her down, since they have no proof. Wei then orders Swire's squad to purge the remaining Reunion forces in a single day without help from Rhodes Island. Speculation (no source found yet): He fears the attacks are part of a larger plot by the Ursus Empire."
    ],
