    "id": "episode-07-the-birth-of-tragedy",
    "title": "Episode 07: The Birth of Tragedy",
    "type": "Main story",
    "when": "Chapter 7",
    "summary": "Talulah turns Chernobog's core toward Lungmen. Ch'en renounces the city, Rhodes Island breaks into Chernobog, and Patriot dies, with Amiya revealed as the new Lord of Fiends. Some supporting details are speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "Kal'tsit tells Wei's office that Talulah has detached Chernobog's core plate and set it on a direct course for Lungmen. Chernobog is still officially an Ursus city, so a collision could start a war between Ursus and Yan. At the same time, W tries to assassinate Talulah in the control tower with Originium explosives, but Talulah weakens the blast with her Arts. Cornered, W detonates the explosives strapped to her own body and is seemingly killed. Disputed: the draft said W fakes her death by jumping from the tower. Sources say she detonates explosives on her body instead. Talulah then gives one of the override keys to Patriot.",
      "Islam Witte, the speaker of Ursus's parliament, confirms that the Ursus government will not stop the collision. Disputed: the draft called him Ursus's Minister of Finance and Wei's friend. Sources give his title as speaker, and the friendship is not confirmed. Speculation (no source found yet): Messengers on both sides have been attacked for what they know. Ch'en announces that she will go to Chernobog and face Talulah herself, and she and Wei argue. Speculation: A member of the Shadow Guard offers to go in and die fighting for Lungmen. Ch'en declares that she is Infected, unleashes Chi Xiao on the Shadow Guard, and turns in her badge. The Shadow Guard blocks the blast, and Ch'en jumps out of a window to escape. Speculation: The drop is hundreds of meters. She severs her ties to Lungmen and to her uncle.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Wei issues a secret arrest warrant for Ch'en. Hoshiguma intercepts her and says it should be Wei Yenwu who dies for Lungmen, not Ch'en. Ch'en confesses that she is Infected, a fact she had hidden from her partner for three years, and that Talulah is her sister. Hoshiguma refuses to let her die for nothing. They struggle, and Hoshiguma eventually lets her go, knowing she will never see Ch'en again. Speculation: Ch'en cuts through Hoshiguma's shield, Hannya.",
      "Wei dismisses the Shadow Guards, which keeps them from going after Ch'en. Speculation (no source found yet): Fumizuki tries to bring Ch'en back. Wei decides to attack Chernobog himself, so that he can atone for his mistakes if he dies there. Kal'tsit proposes that Rhodes Island fight Reunion instead. As an independent company of Infected, Rhodes Island can fight without starting a war, and Wei reluctantly agrees that Lungmen will not interfere with Rhodes Island's operations. Before leaving, Kal'tsit asks for the remains of Edward Artorius, Talulah's late father.",
      "Rhodes Island infiltrates Chernobog. Dobermann's team uses the Bad Guy VTOL to lure the enemies. Nearl, Firewatch, and Elysium use an upcoming sandstorm to hide themselves from enemy detection. Speculation (no source found yet): Amiya, Kal'tsit, Rosmontis, and two Elite Operators reach the city on grappling hooks, and clear a small Reunion patrol. Rosmontis's sudden display of brutal force unsettles the Doctor, who questions why a child has such terrifying power. Speculation: This causes friction with Kal'tsit.",
      "Inside the city, the team finds Guard, the sole survivor of Ace and Scout's final stand in Chernobog. He now serves under Patriot's guerrillas, and they find him comforting an Infected Ursine woman named Tatiana, who accuses Reunion of spreading Oripathy. Guard defends the guerrillas as nothing like the rest of Reunion. He joined Patriot to help the innocent survive, and he credits Patriot's supply work with saving many Ursus citizens. Kal'tsit tells him that Rhodes Island caused FrostNova's death, so they may end up on opposing sides.",
      "At the center of the core city, Amiya, Kal'tsit, and Rosmontis run into Patriot and his elite Guerrilla Shieldguards. Amiya conjures pleasant visions of Patriot's family, but he realizes that Amiya is the next Lord of Fiends and the genuine successor of Theresa, which fulfills the Kazdelian prophecy. He is angered by the illusion and insists that his end is not someone else's to give. Speculation (no source found yet): Patriot bars their path, saying that only those who can defeat him can be trusted to stop Talulah. His Oripathy is worsening, and Rhodes Island's operators finally halt him. Speculation: He entrusts them with the key Talulah gave him.",
      "As he dies, Patriot's body freezes in place, his hands stretched out toward Amiya. Disputed: the draft said he moves to crush her skull in his final rage, and that Amiya stands firm while he dies standing. Sources say he dies reaching for her. Speculation (no source found yet): Patriot's death was prophesied at the hands of the Sarkaz King. Snow begins to fall at the same moment that Rhodes Island cremates FrostNova's body.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): The remaining Shieldguards see the snow as a sign from their fallen leaders. They honor their memory and set aside their anger toward Rhodes Island so they can work together against Talulah. Reunion then fractures into civil war. Shieldguard fighters rise against Talulah's followers and proclaim that she has betrayed Patriot and all of Reunion.",
      "Rhodes Island splits up in the chaos. The Doctor and Kal'tsit descend toward the Chernobog Sarcophagus, while Amiya, Rosmontis, and the Shieldguards head for the control tower. The Doctor's group meets a severely wounded W, who accuses them of murder and calls Kal'tsit a lunatic. Kal'tsit has Mon3tr toss W through a wall. Mephisto crawls toward the Sarcophagus, trying to erase his memories. Ch'en reaches the control tower at last, ready to face Talulah. Far away in Londinium, Theresis, Regent of Kazdel, plots to resurrect Theresa."
    ],
