    "id": "episode-08-roaring-flare",
    "title": "Episode 08: Roaring Flare",
    "type": "Main story",
    "when": "Chapter 8",
    "summary": "Talulah's path from a quiet village to Reunion's leader is traced. Amiya and Ch'en break the Black Snake and stop Chernobog. Sources confirm Alina's death and the Black Snake fight, but the operator casualty count is not confirmed. Much of the backstory is speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "Speculation (no source found yet): In 1089, Talulah lived with an elderly couple in a small village in the northwestern Ursus tundra. She had arrived two years earlier with nothing but fancy clothes and a sword, and the couple took her in like a daughter. She became close to Alina, an Elafian girl who also treated the couple as family. One day an Infected Patrol punched the old man, and Talulah drove the patrolmen away with her Arts without killing them. Sources say Talulah was sent to a couple, Ivan Iziaslav and his wife, after she was on the run from Ursus authorities.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): The patrol came back in greater numbers, searching for the attacker. The old man turned himself in to protect Talulah, since he was Infected too. Talulah rushed to save him and was too late. In her rage she killed the patrolmen with fire and sword. Alina revealed that she was Infected too, and the two fled together. Later, Talulah stopped a patrol from slaughtering an unregistered Infected village, and its people chose to follow her.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Talulah's path turned darker after that. Patriot told her that her dreams would only lead the Infected to death at the hands of the Ursus Army, and Alina sent her off with a smile. Later, Patrol retaliation against villages that had traded with Reunion gravely injured Alina. Alina died in Talulah's embrace before she could be brought back to camp. Disputed: the draft said Alina's last words urged Talulah never to give in to hatred. Sources record her last words as an urging to Talulah to live on.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): After the Emperor's Blades spread rumors that split Reunion, many Infected left. Talulah then found that the villagers near a Reunion camp had locked the hungry Infected in an empty granary to starve. She burned the village in fury. Sources say that after Alina's death, Kashchey's influence overpowered Talulah, and she slaughtered villagers and burned a village in her grief. Speculation: Many Infected leave Reunion, unable to trust anyone of noble birth, and each departure wounds Talulah.",
      "In the present, Chernobog's core is a battlefield, with the Guerrillas and Patriot's loyalists fighting Talulah's Sarkaz mercenaries. Rosmontis and Amiya advance on the control tower. Speculation (no source found yet): When loyalists block the way, Rosmontis collapses the building with her Arts. Amiya is prepared to release one of the ten rings Theresa gave her to dampen her power. Along the way she sees more evidence of Ch'en's presence in Chernobog, and a childhood vision of Ch'en.",
      "Rosmontis's squad heads to the sealing layer, the wall that would cut off the control tower for good. Disguised Ursus Third Army troops ambush them, and Bluishsilver dies. Rosmontis tears open the rising wall with her Arts, opening a path for the allied forces, then collapses from exhaustion. Earlier, Guard had proposed a formal alliance with the Shieldguards, and Amiya reached an agreement with their leader.",
      "The Doctor and Kal'tsit advance toward the Sarcophagus, fighting Herdified Sarkaz warriors on the way. Speculation (no source found yet): They find a crystalline beast breathing out concentrated Originium. It is not hostile, but it is in pain, and Kal'tsit kills it to end its suffering. Once the Sarcophagus is powered down, the Doctor recalls a name, Priestess, which leaves Kal'tsit stunned. Meanwhile, Amiya's squad stays behind as she goes alone to confront Talulah. Speculation: She finds the sheath of Chi Xiao, and through Ch'en's lingering presence on it, sees the Originium bomb that infected Ch'en and Nine.",
      "Amiya confronts the Deathless Black Snake, the ideology that had taken hold of Talulah under Kashchey's influence. Speculation (no source found yet): Talulah recognizes Amiya as the King of Sarkaz. Disputed: the draft said Amiya summons the Wrathful Cerulean Flame. Sources say Amiya forms a black blade modeled on Ch'en's Chi Xiao, which resembles Kollam's Wrathful Cerulean Flame. She fights alongside Ch'en, and after a hard battle they break through Talulah's defenses. Speculation (no source found yet): Overwhelmed by guilt, Talulah thinks about taking her own life, but Ch'en and Amiya's intervention leads her to choose to keep living.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): W tries to stop Chernobog, but the key Amiya gave her lacks sufficient clearance. Talulah then reveals a true master key she has kept hidden, and the city's advance stops. The Ursus Third Army is routed. Talulah and Ch'en drop their swords and fight with their fists, while W compares Amiya to Theresa. Then the Doctor and Kal'tsit arrive just as Amiya collapses. Kal'tsit uses the Doctor's blood to stabilize her, as she has done before.",
      "The Bad Guy takes Talulah into custody. Speculation (no source found yet): Kal'tsit explains that without Talulah as a bargaining chip, Ursus and Yan could destroy Rhodes Island. W leaves with her mercenaries, and Rosmontis says goodbye to the Shieldguards. Disputed: the draft said the crisis cost forty-one Rhodes Island operators, including Ace and Scout. Sources do not confirm this count. Ace and Scout died earlier in Chernobog. Speculation: The total loss is forty-one operators. Afterward Wei Yenwu and Ch'en meet at the graves of Talulah's father and Ch'en's mother. Speculation (no source found yet): This is their first meeting since the disaster. Ch'en stays with Rhodes Island for now."
    ],
