    "id": "under-tides",
    "title": "Under Tides",
    "type": "Event",
    "when": "Event, 2021",
    "summary": "Skadi follows Gladiia to the Iberian town of Sal Viento, where a cult's sacrifices and a church catacomb reveal that she and the Abyssal Hunters carry Seaborn blood. Some details are speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "Confirmed: Skadi hears a song sung by a fellow Aegir that feels wrong to her, and she finds Gladiia, an Abyssal Hunter thought to be dead, taking Specter away. Confirmed: Gladiia invites Skadi to follow to Sal Viento, a nomadic city in Iberia. Disputed: the draft described Sal Viento as a lethargic coastal town. The source calls it a nomadic city. Confirmed: A Liberi named Anita offers to guide Skadi, and she learns that the town expects a gift from the ocean at the hundredth high tide, with one of its people chosen as an offering.",
      "Confirmed: That night, Inquisitor Irene arrives and treats Skadi as a heretic because she is an Aegir, and attacks her. Confirmed: High Inquisitor Dario fights Skadi too, but sea creatures interrupt the battle. Confirmed: Skadi and Irene fight the creatures together until dawn. Confirmed: Afterward, Skadi argues with Irene over whether the townsfolk should eat the remains, and she leaves in anger.",
      "Confirmed: On the shore, the Inquisitors find that the chosen one has been given to the Seaborn as a sacrifice. Confirmed: Sacrifices that have turned into Seaborn attack Skadi and Anita, and Skadi drives them off and recovers her harp. Confirmed: That night she plays an Aegirian song, and the high tide arrives with food from the sea, just as the townsfolk had been told.",
      "Confirmed: The bishop Quintus and Gladiia address the crowd, and Quintus leads Skadi and Gladiia down into the church's catacombs. Confirmed: There, Specter is held in a water tank. Confirmed: Quintus admits he belongs to the Church of the Deep, an Aegirian cult that worships the Seaborn, and that he experimented on Specter to learn the secrets of the Abyssal Hunters. Confirmed: Gladiia attacks him in anger, but a humanoid Seaborn called The First To Talk strikes her down.",
      "Confirmed: The First tells Skadi that she and the Abyssal Hunters carry Seaborn blood, which makes them Aegir-Seaborn hybrids. Confirmed: Skadi is torn, and begins to accept that she is bound to the Seaborn in blood. Confirmed: Gladiia rises again and strikes The First, interrupting the process.",
      "Confirmed: In the flooded catacombs, Gladiia kills The First, and Specter breaks free from her tank. Confirmed: Quintus transforms into a Seaborn leviathan, but the Hunters defeat him. Confirmed: Kal'tsit arrives with Mon3tr, destroys the church, and buries the remaining sea monsters in its ruins. Confirmed: She agrees to be held in Iberia so that the Hunters can leave freely. Confirmed: Back at Rhodes Island, Gladiia resolves to find the lost Iberian dreadnought Stultifera Navis."
    ],
