      "Confirmed: A burning wreck falls into the Triton chemical plant in Trimounts, and the military learns it was a prototype test flight of the H.A.M.H.R.R. Confirmed: The Tin Man and Saria examine the wreck and find evidence of Kristen's involvement. Disputed: the draft said Silence follows a Transmitter to the crash site and finds that evidence. The source says Silence is searching for a stolen Transmitter there, and that Jara Wilson of Rhine Lab rescued her from a soldier.",
      "Confirmed: Ho'olheyak, an agent of the Maylander Foundation, interferes at every step, including an ambush on Muelsyse while she searches Control's office. Speculation (no source found yet): Muelsyse invites the Doctor to help track Kristen, and the two share a quiet dance in her vivarium.",
      "Confirmed: Ferdinand Clooney discovers that the project draws energy from an unknown source, and he deceives Blake about the launch. Confirmed: The military plans to assassinate Vice President Jackson, and a planted bomb destroys a street during his tour. Confirmed: Saria is shot in the head by a sniper on Blake's orders, and Jara rescues her. Speculation (no source found yet): The Tin Man recruits Rhodes Island to stop the plot.",
      "Confirmed: Ho'olheyak kills the Tin Man with Nasti Lunorey's help and sets the Doctor up to take the blame. Confirmed: The Doctor turns out to be a water clone of Muelsyse. Disputed: the draft said Silence makes a deal with Ferdinand and agrees to lead the military to Kristen. The source says a Liberi injects herself with a Transmitter and makes that deal. Confirmed: Silence amplifies the Transmitter's signal, but her aircraft crashes.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Kristen and Ahrens Parvis assemble a new Transmitter hub. Confirmed: Kal'tsit tracks the power source of the H.A.M.H.R.R. Confirmed: The Preserver, a simulated consciousness, reveals hundreds of thousands of dormant Sarcophagi and has diverted the facility's power to help Kristen pierce the Starpod. Speculation (no source found yet): Kal'tsit and the Doctor head to the source together.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Kristen predicts Saria's moves and sends her out through an emergency hatch. Disputed: the draft said the Galleria Stellaria fires its built-up energy. The source says the H.A.M.H.R.R.'s Arc-01 fires, tearing a hole in the Starpod that reveals the Twin Moons to Terra for the first time in thousands of years. Confirmed: The Preserver is Trevor Friston, and at his request Kal'tsit erases his emotional data so he can die as his original self. Confirmed: Friston passes away.",
