    "id": "who-is-real",
    "title": "Who is Real",
    "type": "Side story",
    "when": "Late autumn to early winter 1101 (Hui-ch'i Incident)",
    "summary": "Lava and Kroos are drawn into P'o-shan, a painted village, where they learn the truth of Sui, Nian, and Dusk, and Saga escapes to Rhodes Island. No source was reached for this entry; all of its story is unverified.",
    "body": [
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Lava and Kroos, sent by Nian to find her sister Dusk, are rescued in the Yan wilderness near Mount Hui-ch'i by a Liberi fortune teller calling himself Mr. Nothing. An old cottage opens into P'o-shan, a village where the sun and the moons coexist and there is no true night. The trio befriend Saga, a Higashinese nun, and meet Dawn, a pawnshop keeper.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): At night, creatures the villagers call Ink Spirits attack. After a fierce battle the village is destroyed, and the dead are left behind. The next morning the village is rebuilt, the dead are restored, and all memory of the attack is gone. Saga and Dawn reveal that the gang is inside a painted world made by Dusk. Dawn reveals the Ink Spirits' weakness: firecrackers.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): When Lava speaks Nian's name in the storyteller's hearing, Dusk traps each of them in a painted world drawn from their own memories. Lava is left alone in a void, where Nian gathers everyone and tells the legend of Sui, a Feranmut who betrayed its kin and shattered into twelve fragments, the siblings including Nian and Dusk.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Nian asks Dusk to help reunite the fragments of Sui, but Dusk refuses. Nian's dimensional firecracker shatters the painted worlds and returns everyone to the real world, destroying Dusk's cottage. Saga escapes her own painted world by her own will, and convinces Dusk to join Nian. Saga leaves the group and reaches Rhodes Island.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Dusk later stays at Rhodes Island, linked to the landship through her painted world. She remembers Dawn's dying wish, that she recreate P'o-shan inside a painting, and she fulfils it."
    ],
