    "id": "episode-17-critical-phase-transition",
    "title": "Episode 17: Critical Phase Transition",
    "type": "Main story",
    "when": "Chapter 17",
    "summary": "Kal'tsit is restored from Zelgrad's Sarcophagus. The First Army's Infected fuel program is exposed, and Fyodor dissolves the legislature. Some details are speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "Speculation (no source found yet): After the Far North Rebellion, Rhodes Island recovers at New Rhodes Island. Amiya confides in Civilight Eterna about her grief over losing Kal'tsit, and asks it to keep her worsening vital signs from the Doctor. Closure's resurrection simulations keep failing. In Ursus, the First Army captures Hierda and her followers. Marshal Svetlana orders Hierda to heal her infected son, Anatoliy, in exchange for protecting her companions. Hierda restores Anatoliy's painless state, and he takes her along as his doctor.",
      "In Deity Grypherburg, Dur-nar's intelligence shows that Originium leaves the city for Zelgrad every day, even though Ursus is short on it. Confirmed: the government sent vast daily Originium reserves through concealed shipping routes destined for Project Zero, and it moved the Sarcophagus from Deity Grypherburg to Zelgrad for study. Disputed: the draft called Zelgrad a satellite city of Deity Grypherburg. The source calls it one of the satellite cities of an unknown larger city. Zelgrad is a closed district, which Rhodes Island finds suspicious. Chairman Witte says Ursus will not survive winter unless the Sarcophagus becomes an energy source, so Rhodes Island agrees to cooperate. In exchange for research access, it supplies data that unlocks in segments once the team leaves Zelgrad. Speculation (no source found yet): Witte writes a letter of safe passage.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Marshal Evgeny forces Scioppa to march on Zelgrad by threatening his lieutenant Sirka, who is secretly in the city to assassinate Anatoliy. At the admission post, Raidian claims the team is a medical research team, and Amiya vouches for Tulin's miners. In an underground clinic, Dr. Nadezhda tends Kirill, whose body is failing, and Hierda's Arts replace it with Originium crystals. Tonya, whose sister Nina was infected by a contaminated jacket, also arrives. Raidian's interception attempt causes an Arts overload, and the team concludes Zelgrad hides an unknown disease.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): The First Army raids the clinic. Kirill dies and the soldiers take him and Nina. Tonya plants a bomb to board a truck heading for the wall, and Closure saves her from pursuit with her drones. The group meets Red of Reunion and then Tulin's miners, who hide them in Zelgrad's underground layer. Closure is shocked to find Talulah there with Sirka. Crownslayer reveals a factory on a hidden expansion plate. Inside, dozens of butchered Infected and non-Infected bodies, with Originium clusters growing out of them, sit in glass vats. Disputed in part: the sources say the First Army kidnapped Infected residents for experiments on the Originium in their bodies. The source does not say the bodies were used as coolant, so that conclusion is speculation (no source found yet).",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Tonya finds Nina's blanket and weeps. Tulin speaks to the Zelgradians about the disease and the experiments, and the people walk out together. At the research institute, Alita Valueva, director of the Zelgrad lab, explains that the Sarcophagus is overheating and cannot be cooled. Partly confirmed: the source lists her as the daughter of Lada Valueva, whose page links to Gummy, so Amiya's realization that Alita is Gummy's mother is plausible. The source does not name a New Lab Six. Speculation (no source found yet): Alita shuts off the lights to let the team into the Sarcophagus chamber, then soldiers kill her. She had discovered that thousands of dismembered Infected were feeding the Sarcophagus. Mon3tr finds that brute-force attempts to break Kal'tsit's lockdown have badly damaged it, and it is nearing critical.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Monsters pour out of the Sarcophagus core. Anatoliy kills scientists who are searching for the research data, and Hierda stops him again, telling him to prove he is more than a tool. Amiya uses the Black Crown to suppress the Sarcophagus's energy while Closure traces a backdoor program. The Doctor witnesses Kal'tsit's memories, and finds her core code. Mon3tr and Closure extract it. A small mechanical house with legs, which calls itself a hen, emerges and joins them as GALLUS². Klim Valuev, listed as Alita's husband, stays behind to redirect the energy toward the Central Governorate, and the weaponization module melts.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Sechin reaches Zelgrad. Scioppa turns the Volnov, Sechin's flagship, into the Fourth Army's frigate and rams it, then Sirka bargains with Svetlana and Anatoliy for a ceasefire in exchange for her surrender. She reveals that she is Evgeny's father's illegitimate daughter, and tells Anatoliy they are half-siblings. The First Army withdraws, and the Zelgrad gates open at sunset. Tulin confesses to Crownslayer that she is really Milana, a miner who took the name of the author Ivan Tulin after the real Tulin was killed. Anatoliy later stabs Svetlana, and when Hierda leaves him, he dies alone of Oripathy.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): In Deity Grypherburg, Witte suspects Vice Chairman Vasily Gorchikov of working with the pro-war faction. Eloysius finds military-issue supplies at the Rhodes Island treatment center for Far North refugees, and an Emperor's Blade threatens to clear it out until Hellagur drives him back. Eloysius finds her father's letter requesting a transfer for Platon Lunin. Platon admits her father has joined the pro-war faction, and Eloysius kills him. Witte reports this to Tsar Fyodor, and Vasily is suspended. The Fourth Army crosses the Second Army's lines toward Zelgrad, and Fyodor vows to lead the Central Army himself if civil war comes.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): At the citizen's forum, the so-called citizen representatives turn out to be actors, nobles, and wealthy children. Vetochki speaks for The Winter Emergency Resource Allocation Act, asking only that people not die of cold. The nobles mock her, and Fyodor declares the Act law and dissolves both the State Council and the Imperial Duma. Meanwhile Grand Duchess Elisabeth summons the Yurodstvo through an Elafian Shaman, anchored into Anastasia, Fyodor's supposed older sister. The false Anastasia calls herself the Grand Princess and feeds starving crowds. Confirmed: the coffin is the size of an infant and holds no body. Disputed: the draft said Fyodor finds a coffin engraved with Anastasia's name beside his mother's grave. The source says Fyodor told Witte to dig up Anastasia's supposed grave. The source lists Anastasia as a possible sister whose veracity is unknown, not as an older sister.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Closure's resurrection process works, and Kal'tsit is reborn. She reprimands the Doctor for the danger, but is grateful. She stores AMa-10's core code as an administrator program in the Sarcophagus, so she will have no next life. Rhodes Island's rebuilt landship now has a regional Originium stasis machine. Kal'tsit says Priestess planted the source code in Zelgrad. The Doctor finally understands the message left in the Far North mines: a debate about civilization that has lasted for millennia. Rhodes Island must prove that the civilization of today has the potential to survive, and that it has value."
    ],
