    "id": "break-the-ice",
    "title": "Break the Ice",
    "type": "Side story",
    "when": "Kjerag, the Snow Realm (Holy Hunt and Grand Ceremony)",
    "summary": "A Holy Hunt ends in a poisoning and a rigged accusation, and the Doctor helps Enya descend Mount Karlan to end the civil war in Kjerag. Some details are speculation with no source found yet.",
    "body": [
      "Confirmed: The Tri-Clan Council meets at the sacred temple atop Mount Karlan. Karlan Trade's Chief Technical Officer, Gnosis Edelweiss, has been mining the holy mountain illegally and attacked an inspection team. Speculation (no source found yet): Enciodes Silverash fired him, and the clan leaders Arctosz Paleroche and Ratatos Browntail demand the Silverashes give up their territory. Confirmed: Enciodes agrees on one condition: all the clans' territory passes to the Saintess, his estranged sister Enya. Speculation (no source found yet): The Paleroches and Browntails accept.",
      "Speculation (no source found yet): Enciodes invites the Doctor to Kjerag to fill Gnosis's vacated post. The Doctor arrives with Ensia Silverash and Karlan Trade staff, guarded by Aurora and Sharp. They are drawn into surveying the factories and overseeing the handover, watched by the Paleroche generals Gulo and Valais. Confirmed: Gnosis tips off Ratatos Browntail to a secret Silverash smuggling bridge, then destroys it with Originium explosives, derailing the train so the Browntails can capture the elite soldiers aboard.",
      "Confirmed: On the day before the Grand Ceremony, the clans hold the Holy Hunt. Confirmed: An assassin named Monch tries to kill Enciodes and fails. Confirmed: Sciurus Browntail recognizes Monch as her own subordinate and rushes to defend her, which implicates the Browntails. Confirmed: The Great Elder orders Sciurus arrested. Disputed: the draft said Sciurus collapsed into a coma from poison. The source says the Great Elder is the one poisoned, after drinking wine the Paleroches presented as tribute.",
      "Confirmed: Enciodes publicly accuses both clans of plotting to overturn the Tri-Clan Council. Speculation (no source found yet): Gnosis appears, claims to act for the Browntails, and is subdued by Enciodes's bodyguard Degenbrecher. Confirmed: Enciodes summons his Tschäggättäs, a unit trained in Victoria, to capture the two clan heads. Confirmed: The Doctor anticipates the move and sends Sharp to intervene. Speculation (no source found yet): Ratatos and Arctosz escape. Confirmed: Yucatan, Sciurus's husband, is captured while trying to rescue her.",
      "Confirmed: Enciodes and Gnosis staged the feud to discredit the two clans. Gnosis also arranged the Great Elder's poisoning, which pushed General Valais to act on her grudge against the Vine-Bead Court. Speculation (no source found yet): Enciodes's goal is to make the Silverashes the sole rulers of Kjerag and accelerate its industrialization. Confirmed: After the ceremony, several Browntail villages defect to the Silverashes. Confirmed: Ratatos traps herself and Enciodes in a burning building, and both are rescued by Degenbrecher and Sciurus.",
      "Confirmed: The Paleroches turn to Rhodes Island. Speculation (no source found yet): The Doctor agrees to stop the civil war. Confirmed: The plan is for Arctosz and the Doctor to lead an army up Mount Karlan to rescue Enya, while Gulo's forces take the neighboring pass. Confirmed: Ensia, after receiving the Doctor's message, slips past the soldiers and climbs the mountain alone. Speculation (no source found yet): Ensia was warned by Aurora. Confirmed: In the temple, the dying Great Elder begs Enya to uphold the faith. Speculation (no source found yet): Enya replies that Kjerag has stagnated and the people need reform.",
      "Confirmed: With encouragement from Ensia and the head maid Kjera, Enya decides to descend the mountain and confront her brother. Confirmed: Kjera, the avatar of Kjeragandr, performs a miracle that stops the blizzard, and the warriors lay down their arms. Speculation (no source found yet): The three clans bow to Enya. Speculation (no source found yet): Enya opens Kjerag to foreign believers, Arctosz resigns, and the Browntails sign a subordination agreement. Confirmed: The Silverashes take over leadership of the Tri-Clan Council. Confirmed: Gnosis becomes Enciodes's representative on Rhodes Island. Speculation (no source found yet): Enciodes apologizes to the Doctor for using them in his scheme."
    ],
