      "Confirmed: Lin Qingyan follows a lead about the missing Yun Qingping to Mangshan Town, at the foot of Mt. Mang. She finds a secret deal set for a teahouse, where a kung fu tome attributed to Chongyue is to change hands. Confirmed: The tea server, Hu Jun, poisons the group to get the tome for himself. He flees with it, and when he falls from an upper window his body shatters into teapot shards. The tome vanishes.",
      "Confirmed: Mr. Pu, who runs the town school and settles local disputes, explains that many townsfolk are geists born from Feranmut influence, shaped by the nearby Tomb of Sui. Confirmed: Rumors of a tome that can make geists true humans have stirred unrest. Disputed: the draft said Lin Qingyan returns Hu Jun's remains to the teacher. The source says Mr. Pu stole the pouch of remains, which held only pebbles, and later attacked Lin with animated household objects.",
      "Confirmed: Lin Qingyan is called to Master Wan, a dying merchant whose lucky stone has become a geist. It resents the obsession that drove Master Wan to rebuild his fortune again and again. Confirmed: The stone is returned, and Master Wan gives up his obsession and dies at peace. Confirmed: The accident was caused by one of Master Wan's children, who tried to break into a cabinet.",
      "Disputed: the draft said Yun Qingping follows an old man to the foot of Mt. Mang. The source says he follows a summons up the mountain with Bai Jin, who is searching for her missing husband, Lan Ke. Confirmed: At an ancient pavilion, Lan Ke, a young Vulpo, is stuck on a weiqi board in a cycle that can only end in a draw. Yun sees the whole board and wins in one move. Confirmed: Lan Ke fades away content, and Bai Jin also finds peace. Confirmed: Liang, a sentient construct, then leads Yun up the mountain. Speculation (no source found yet): Yun meets the woman who summoned him.",
      "Confirmed: Zheng Chou, a retired swordsman, lost his sword, the Delivering Blade, seven years earlier. A nameless swordswoman later challenged him and trained under him. Confirmed: Someone has been using his sword's name for crimes, and the swordswoman is a geist born of his obsession. Confirmed: Lin Qingyan destroys her with Lei Fa, and Huai Tianpei snatches the tome from the ground. Confirmed: Later, the swordswoman returns without her memories and joins Zheng Chou on a new journey.",
      "Confirmed: Mo Yi, a Shanhaizhong member, stole the tome from Yumen's armory and left a challenge for Huai Tianpei. Confirmed: At the peak, Mo Yi reveals that the book is an ordinary, mass-produced copy, and summons a shadow of Shuo, Chongyue's Feranmut aspect. Confirmed: Huai Tianpei fights the shadow and destroys it with a final blow. Disputed: the draft said Yun Qingping tells the crowd the tome holds no magic. The source credits the reveal to Mo Yi. Speculation (no source found yet): Huai Tianpei falls from the cliff afterward.",
      "Confirmed: Zuo Le and Mr. Pu bring the situation under control. Speculation (no source found yet): Zuo Le arrives with troops from Yumen and lets the fighters go. Confirmed: Mo Yi's real aim was to meet Yi, the Sui proxy who oversees the Garden of Grotesqueries, and to find a remnant of Jie, a proxy who vanished a century ago."
