      "Confirmed: On 15 August 1102, a fire destroyed more than 70,000 case files in the Judicial Review Office. Confirmed: Yu Cheng, a former minister and Lin Qingyan's mentor, confessed to the arson although he was in prison at the time. Confirmed: Lin Qingyan traces his last case, a 1062 murder, to Gu Quan, a low-ranking ceremonial officer who died in 1092.",
      "Confirmed: Gu Quan raised his daughter, Blaze, in Victoria, and Blaze is a Rhodes Island operator. Speculation (no source found yet): Blaze is the key witness Lin Qingyan needs. Confirmed: In Baizao, Blaze criticizes the tangerine cakes at Savors at Yu's, which leads to a quarrel with the head chef, Yu, and a bet over finding better cakes. Confirmed: The food critic Xingzhu, who is secretly Ning Yin, guides Blaze around the kitchens. Confirmed: Yu trains Blaze to cook longevity noodles so she can enter a chef selection.",
      "Confirmed: At the selection, Blaze serves her noodles to Mo Bufu, head chef of Ding Feng Lou, who scorns the sugar in tangerine cakes. Confirmed: A kitchen fire breaks out, and Blaze saves him. Confirmed: Mo Bufu reveals that Gu Quan was imprisoned for supporting the Grand Preceptor, a reformer accused of treason. Confirmed: Only Yu Cheng and Ning Shu contacted Gu Quan in prison, and Ning Shu ordered his release. Confirmed: Minister Chen Che warns Lin Qingyan to drop the case, and she resigns quietly.",
