      "Confirmed: Ning Shu reveals the hidden history. During the 1062 coup, the Minister of Justice framed the Grand Preceptor. Confirmed: Gu Quan rescued the infant survivor, Blaze, but was caught and forced to surrender his own newborn daughter instead. Confirmed: Ning Shu raised that child as Ning Yin. Confirmed: Blaze and Ning Yin reunite as sisters. Disputed: the draft said Gu Quan tried to flee the country with the baby. The source says he was caught while trying to save the infant.",
      "Confirmed: Blaze confronts the True Lung in the palace, with Lin Qingyan and Vice Minister Taihe present. Confirmed: The True Lung took the throne after his brother, Yan Wu, fled the capital, and the Grand Preceptor was framed to legitimize his reign. Speculation (no source found yet): Blaze brings him a bowl of longevity noodles and tells him never to forget those who sacrificed themselves. The source does not mention the noodles.",
      "Confirmed: Yu, the youngest fragment of Sui, prepares a feast for his second eldest brother, Wang, and sends him off with a soup symbolizing regret. Confirmed: Wang and Ji arrive at the Tomb of Sui with imperial guards and collect keepsakes from their siblings. Confirmed: At the True Lung's decree, the tomb opens and the final battle against the bestial Sui begins. Speculation (no source found yet): Wang tells Ji to leave so he can settle the matter himself."
